          "line": 275,
          "title": "singleQuoted duplicates the existing shellQuote escaping algorithm",
          "detail": "internal/cli/archive.go:353-355 already defines `shellQuote(s string) string { return \"'\" + strings.ReplaceAll(s, \"'\", `'\\''`) + \"'\" }` for exactly this POSIX single-quote close-escape-reopen technique, with a comment explaining the same rationale repeated almost verbatim in the new singleQuoted's doc comment (internal/brief/brief.go:265-274). The new PRTitleQuoted (internal/brief/brief.go:275-281) reimplements the same one-line escaping rule in a different package instead of sharing it, so a future fix or hardening of the shell-escaping rule (e.g. for control characters) has two independent copies to update.",
          "lenses": [
            "consistency"
          ]
        },
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "internal/brief/templates/run-push_pr.md",
          "line": 4,
          "title": "Body path interpolated unquoted in the same shell command whose title is carefully quoted",
          "detail": "`gh pr create --base {{.Base}} --title '{{.PRTitleQuoted}}' --body-file {{.PRBodyPath}}` quotes the title (via singleQuoted/PRTitleQuoted, added specifically because a shell would otherwise split the command on spaces) but leaves `--body-file {{.PRBodyPath}}` bare. PRBodyPath is finish.PRPath(bdir), an absolute path under the workspace/repo root, which can contain spaces just as much as any other filesystem path — the exact risk internal/cli/archive.go's shellQuote (used for discardSweep's `git clean -fd -- '\u003crel\u003e'`) exists to guard against ('a worktree path is whatever the user's filesystem says — a space in it would otherwise split the command into arguments'). brief.go:279-280 asserts PRBodyPath is safe to interpolate bare 'since it is takt's own \u003cbundle\u003e/finish/pr.md', but that reasoning is exactly what shellQuote's own doc comment rejects for repo/bundle-relative paths. The same command should quote both arguments.",
          "lenses": [
            "consistency"
          ]
        }
      ]
