          "title": "TAKT_FAKE_REVIEW_CALLS log-parsing loop duplicated across two test files",
          "detail": "internal/cli/oploop_test.go:881-891 and internal/cli/close_internal_test.go:324-333 (both added by this same task) contain near-identical logic: split the calls file on newlines, `strings.Cut` each line on the first space to get (rubric, logID), filter by rubric, then `strings.Cut` the matching line again to pull out the LogID for the logs/\u003cid\u003e.prompt read. A small shared helper (e.g. `callsForRubric(t, callsFile, rubric string) []string`) in the cli test package would avoid the two copies drifting (e.g. one trims trailing newline before splitting, the other doesn't need to since it reuses the same TrimRight call — but any future change to the calls-file format must be made in both places).",
